Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||10-23-2000||01:14 AM||||Hi, I was checking out a Fiat Spider 2000 today and it looks really good, except it won't start.  The guy told me it started last year when he bought it, but it won't start after a year of storage.  It turns over nicely, but just won't start.  Does this sound like a starter or starter solenoid problem?  Or could it be something else?  I think I could get either one for very cheap, but I have no idea what the problem could be if it isn't the starter.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||10-23-2000||02:39 PM||||I had a 81 Fiat 124 Spyder...I loved it...wouldn't mind getting another one someday. But I always had trouble with the carbs on it. Try putting some gas down the carb and see if she starts...might just need primed.<P>F ix  I t  A gain  T ony ||||reg||4
Z||000002||JohnnyK||10-23-2000||05:46 PM||||Well, it's not the starter or solonoid (if it's turning over, not the problem). However, check for spark and gas. To check for spark, pull a plug wire, stick a screwdriver into it and place it next to a good grounding point and turn the engine over.. Should see it spark. (Don't grab the metal on teh screwdriver.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||10-25-2000||02:01 AM||||Electrical problems were rampant in 80s Fiats. I couldn't use the radio, headlights, and wipers all at the same time on my 1980 <BR>X 1/9. I loved the car though. Lots of fun to drive when it was running. Would I buy another one? Probably not.||||reg||1
